  "solution": "Given: \n\nIf x⁴+(1)/(x⁴)=1154, where x > 0,\n\nConcept used:\n\n(a + b)2 = a2 + b2 + 2ab\n\n(a + b)³ = a³ + b³ + 3ab(a + b).\n\nCalculations:\n\nAccording to the question,\n\n[x2 + ((1)/(x))2]2 = [(x)4 + ((1)/(x))4] + 2(x2)((1)/(x))2 \n\n⇒ [x2 + ((1)/(x))2]2 = [1154] + 2 \n\n⇒ [x2 + ((1)/(x))2]2 = 1156\n\n⇒ x2 + ((1)/(x))2 = sqrt{1156} = 34\n\nAgain applying the same identity\n\n[x + (1)/(x)]2 = [(x)2 + ((1)/(x))2] + 2(x)((1)/(x))\n\n⇒ [x + (1)/(x)]2 = [34] + 2\n\n⇒ [x + (1)/(x)] = sqrt{36}\n\n⇒ [x + (1)/(x)] = 6\n\nApplying the cube identity\n\n[x + (1)/(x)]3 = [(x)3 + ((1)/(x))3] + 3(x)((1)/(x))(x + (1)/(x))\n\n⇒ [6]³ = [(x)3 + ((1)/(x))3] + 3(6)\n\n⇒ [(x)3 + ((1)/(x))3] = 216 - 18\n\n⇒ [(x)3 + ((1)/(x))3] = 198\n\n**∴ The value of x³+(1)/(x³) is 198.**",
